# A form of football played mainly in [[Ireland]]; teams of 15 [[player]]s [[kick]] or [[punch]] a [[ball]] towards [[goal]]s at each end of a [[grass]] [[pitch]] Gaelic football is also known as Gaelic,  Bogball, and Paddyball, terms that are now widely used to describe the game of Gaelic football. The game of Gaelic is played predominantly by the Catholics population of Ireland , this is due to the close links and support the GAA, the governing body of the sport gives to both Irish Nationalism and the Catholic Church.
